## SQ-EFB-05 (water, lakes)
@phase long
@group B
@commands check the scratch toml has `[worldgen.earth_fill] maxWaterSurplus = 0.5` (instance value since 2026-11-02); lake / river square (the SQ-EF-09 kind, `/locate biome minecraft:river` near plains), Chunky r 300; `grep -E 'too wet\|wet only\|footprint'`; `/cdevtest under` tiles
@pass kept starts: `water-below` only with `max` 2 or less (`waterReach`; deeper water under earth counts, and over `maxOverWater` 24 the start goes), `base water 0` (no flooded floor) except `wet_ok` and pond structures; every `too wet` start has no probe line; no kept start has footprint water above 1.5 x its ground (60:40 passes, 61:39 goes) in its log line; record how many kept starts sit between 50:50 and 60:40 (kept at 0.5, canceled at 0.0)
@fails water under a kept piece deeper than 2: `waterReach` not read (toml key missing, fallback) or the piece has no earth (add its base to `stone_base` / `sand_base`); base water in a house: the ground-level column was counted as ground (E12 lowest-layer rule); a kept start over 60:40: `maxWaterSurplus` not read (still 0.0 or the code default)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
shell grep -nE '^\s*maxWaterSurplus' config/creativeworldgen-common.toml; grep -qE '^\s*maxWaterSurplus = 0\.5' config/creativeworldgen-common.toml
