## SQ-EFB-19 (water reach, live)
@group B, plus a second fresh world (new level-name) with `waterReach = 6`
@commands the SQ-EFB-05 river / lake square and the SQ-EFB-06 coast square in both worlds, Chunky r 300 each; per world: `grep -cE 'CANCELLED' logs/latest.log` over-water lines, `grep -c 'pruned'`, census `/cwglocate census 96 <x> <z>` village and outpost counts; `/cdevtest under` tiles in the 2 world
@pass world 2: every kept start `water-below max` 2 or less under its earth; more over-water cancels and prunes than world 6 (record both counts and the share of villages lost near water; flag to the owner if villages drop by more than a third in the river square); the kept villages near rivers stand on filled banks, no house on a 3+ deep fill (LOOK one from the water)
@fails no difference between worlds: the value is not read per start (`EarthFill.reach()`); villages lost wholesale instead of pruned: `pruneMaxHanging` 8 now trips on water (pieces dropped) and the start still cancels, give the lines
@draft compares two fresh worlds booted with different tomls (waterReach 2 and 6): two boots, which one row cannot hold; per world run the SQ-EFB-05 and -06 steps (/cdevtest under tiles, efb_judge.py under --fail deepwater, efb_judge.py log summary, /cwglocate census 96), then compare the two worlds' counts in the run doc
## SQ-EFB-20 (sand base, tags)
@group B
@commands `/cdevtest tag block creativeworldgen:earth_fill/sand_base`; `grep -i 'item_dict\|philips_sand' logs/latest.log` at startup; `/reload` then read `[earth-fill] blocks:` warnings
@pass the block tag lists the 8 `forge:sandstone` blocks, the terracottas and the 3 Philip's blocks; no unresolved-key warning for `philips_sand_stone_brick`, `philips_red_sand_stone_brick`, `philips_sandstone_tiles`; no `holds no block` warning
@fails Philip's ids renamed in the jar: fix the keys in `item_dict.js` (startup, restart)
@reviewed 2026-11-16
> cdevtest tag block creativeworldgen:earth_fill/sand_base
expect verb=tag kind=block tag=creativeworldgen:earth_fill/sand_base n=\d+ (?=.*[=,]minecraft:sandstone\b)(?=.*[=,]minecraft:red_sandstone\b)(?=.*[=,]minecraft:terracotta\b)(?=.*[=,]philipsruins:sand_stone_brick\b)(?=.*[=,]philipsruins:red_sand_stone_brick\b)(?=.*[=,]philipsruins:sandstone_tiles\b)
bootreject (?i)(unresolved|unknown|missing|not found).*philips_(sand_stone_brick|red_sand_stone_brick|sandstone_tiles)
> reload
sleep 20
reject \[earth-fill\] blocks: .*(holds no block|is not a tag id)
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=tag .*done=0
## SQ-EFB-21 (sand base, counted)
@phase long
@group B
@commands a desert square with villages and a river or oasis (`/locate biome minecraft:desert`, `terralith:desert_oasis`), and a badlands square (`/locate structure towns_and_towers:village_badlands`); Chunky r 300 each; `grep -E 'village_desert\|fortified_desert\|village_badlands\|village_wooded_badlands\|pillager_outpost_desert\|pillager_outpost_badlands\|desert_structures\|badlands_start_dungeon\|village_temple' logs/latest.log`; `/cdevtest under` tiles
@pass their lines show earth counts that include the sandstone / terracotta floor (a T&T badlands village logs hundreds of earth, not 0 to 16; size medium or larger); a house over a river or a cliff now logs over water / air and is pruned or the start canceled; kept ones: `over6 0`, water-below max 2
@fails earth still near 0: the structure tag did not load (`earth_fill.js`, `/reload`) or `withBases` not reached; check `/zq` that the structure is in `#creativeworldgen:earth_fill/sand_base`
@reviewed 2026-11-16
