## SQ-EFB-22 (deserts still work)
@group B, both worlds of SQ-EFB-19
@commands in the desert and badlands squares compare the two worlds: census counts of `minecraft:village_desert`, `terralith:fortified_desert_village`, `towns_and_towers:village_badlands`, the desert and badlands outposts, `minecraft:desert_pyramid`, `betterdeserttemples:desert_temple`; `grep -c` CANCELLED per id
@pass dry desert (no water near): the same count within 10 % in both worlds (sandstone counted makes the size larger, so the air and mound limits grow with it); losses only at water and cliffs, each with a line naming over water / air; desert pyramids judged by their footprint as before; Better Desert Temples and the desert mimic unchanged (not in the tag); LOOK at 2 kept desert villages by an oasis: houses on sand banks, no floor over water
@fails dry-desert villages lost: the larger earth count pushed a mound or air limit (sandstone floors on dunes), give the size and mound numbers; consider `sizes` or an override for `village_desert`
@draft compares the census and CANCELLED counts of the two SQ-EFB-19 worlds (two boots, one row cannot hold them); per world: the SQ-EFB-21 squares, /cwglocate census 96 at each, efb_judge.py log --id the desert and badlands ids; the comparison and the oasis LOOK go in the run doc
